{"textId": {"genre": "L", "category": 1, "index": 4}, "classification": "Ancient", "stage": "Old Babylonian", "version": "", "name": "IM", "order": 40, "manuscripts": [{"id": 1, "siglumDisambiguator": "1", "oldSigla": [], "museumNumber": "IM.21180.X", "accession": "", "periodModifier": "None", "period": "Old Babylonian", "provenance": "Babylonia", "type": "Library", "notes": "", "colophon": "", "unplacedLines": "", "references": [{"id": "RN39Bot", "type": "TRANSLATION", "pages": "250", "notes": "", "linesCited": [], "document": {"id": "RN39Bot", "author": [{"family": "Bottéro", "given": "Jean"}], "title": "L'épopée de Gilgameš", "publisher": "Gallimard", "publisher-place": "Paris", "type": "book", "citation-label": "RN39Bot", "issued": {"date-parts": [[1992]]}}}, {"id": "LS320Dijk", "type": "COPY", "pages": "no. 46", "notes": "", "linesCited": [], "document": {"id": "LS320Dijk", "author": [{"family": "Dijk", "given": "Johannes J.A.", "non-dropping-particle": "van"}], "title": "Texts of Varying Contents", "publisher": "Brill", "publisher-place": "Leiden", "type": "book", "citation-label": "LS320Dijk", "issued": {"date-parts": [[1976]]}}}, {"id": "RN580", "type": "TRANSLATION", "pages": "138-40", "notes": "", "linesCited": [], "document": {"id": "RN580", "author": [{"given": "R.J.", "family": "Tournay"}, {"given": "Aaron", "family": "Shaffer"}], "title": "L'Épopée de Gilgamesh", "publisher": "Les Éditions du Cerf", "publisher-place": "Paris", "type": "book", "citation-label": "RN580", "issued": {"date-parts": [[1994]]}}}, {"id": "westenholz_gilgamesh_1997", "type": "TRANSLATION", "pages": "145", "notes": "", "linesCited": [], "document": {"id": "westenholz_gilgamesh_1997", "publisher-place": "Copenhagen", "title": "Gilgamesh, Enuma Elish: guder og mennesker i oldtidens Babylon", "publisher": "Spektrum", "author": [{"family": "Westenholz", "given": "Ulla"}, {"family": "Westenholz", "given": "Aage"}], "type": "book", "citation-label": "westenholz_gilgamesh_1997", "issued": {"date-parts": [[1997]]}}}, {"id": "RN117", "type": "COPY", "pages": "pl. 14–15", "notes": "", "linesCited": [], "document": {"id": "RN117", "author": [{"family": "George", "given": "Andrew R."}], "title": "The Babylonian Gilgamesh Epic. Introduction, Critical Edition and Cuneiform Texts", "publisher": "Oxford University Press", "publisher-place": "Oxford", "container-title-short": "BGE", "type": "book", "citation-label": "RN117", "issued": {"date-parts": [[2003]]}}}, {"id": "RN117", "type": "EDITION", "pages": "268–271", "notes": "", "linesCited": [], "document": {"id": "RN117", "author": [{"family": "George", "given": "Andrew R."}], "title": "The Babylonian Gilgamesh Epic. Introduction, Critical Edition and Cuneiform Texts", "publisher": "Oxford University Press", "publisher-place": "Oxford", "container-title-short": "BGE", "type": "book", "citation-label": "RN117", "issued": {"date-parts": [[2003]]}}}, {"id": "LS297", "type": "PHOTO", "pages": "pl. 80", "notes": "Obverse only", "linesCited": [], "document": {"id": "LS297", "author": [{"family": "Dijk", "given": "Johannes J.A.", "non-dropping-particle": "van"}], "title": "Cuneiform Texts. Texts of Varying Content", "publisher": "Brill", "publisher-place": "Leiden", "collection-title": "Texts in the Iraq Museum", "container-title-short": "TIM", "collection-number": "9", "type": "book", "citation-label": "LS297", "issued": {"date-parts": [[1969]]}}}], "joins": [], "isInFragmentarium": false}], "uncertainFragments": [], "lines": [{"number": "1", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "1", "atf": "[x x x x x x x x x x x]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": "The first fifteen lines are too damaged to yield very much, but at the beginning Gilgameš and Enkidu appear to be walking hand in hand in the Cedar Forest (ll. 3–4). In ll. 6 ff. one of them is speaking. A badly damaged passage of narrative follows, in which someone is killed. If it is Huwawa then we must accept that this account of his death is very different from that found in OB Ishchali. Otherwise it may be one of his household. From l. 17 to the bottom of the tablet the text is much easier to decipher. As in OB Ishchali Gilgameš and Enkidu go deep into the heart of the forest, violating its sanctity as the home of the gods. Enkidu praises Gilgameš for his feat of arms and asks him to fell a mighty cedar (20–1). From this cedar he intends to make a door for Enlil’s temple in Nippur, and Enlil and his people will be delighted (22–9)."}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […]"}, {"number": "2", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...] | ubbalūnim", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "2", "atf": "[x x x x x x] u₂#-ba#-lu#-nim?#", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] @i{they bring}."}, {"number": "3", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...] | qištim", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "3", "atf": "[x x x x x x] qi₂-iš-tim", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] forest,"}, {"number": "4", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [... | qāt]ī | iṣṣabtū", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "4", "atf": "[x x x x x qa?-t]i iṣ-ṣa-ab-tu", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] they held (hands?)."}, {"number": "5", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...] ... [...] ...", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "5", "atf": "[x x x] ab x [x x] x ha x x-at-tim", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] …"}, {"number": "6", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...] ... | i niwšib | wēdāni", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "6", "atf": "[x x] x-ma i ni#-u₂-ši-ib we-da-ni\n#note: See @bib{RN117@270}: “The variants @i{ni-ú-ši-ib} and @i{ni-ši-ib} for the expected @i{nūšib} seem to suggest an exceptional cohortative @i{i niwšib/nīšib}, analogous with @i{i nipqid}. I assume @i{wēdāni} to be an OB adverb comparable with SB @i{ēdāniš} (@i{Ludlul} I 79). It can be added to the adverbs collected by @bib{farber1982altbabylonische@37–47}; see further @bib{RN1419@198 on 48}.”", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] and let us sit down on our own."}, {"number": "7", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...] ... | kakkab | ...", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "7", "atf": "[x x x] x ka-uk?-ka-ab li-x x x x", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] @i{star}…"}, {"number": "8", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [...] ... | i nīšib | wēdāni", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "8", "atf": "[x x x] x-ma i ni-ši-ib we-da#-ni#", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] and let us sit down on our own."}, {"number": "9", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ... [...] ... | ša erēnim | maṣṣa[r (|) qištim]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "9", "atf": "x [x x] x ša {giš}ERIN ma-ṣa-a[r qi₂-iš-tim]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] of the cedar, the guardian [of the forest,]"}, {"number": "10", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n [... | i]ṣabbassu | [...]\n#note: See @bib{RN117@270}: “Cf. the later line @i{u ārid qištīšu iṣabbassu luʾtu} (SB II 229, 286)?”\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"II\" 229\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"II\" 286\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"II\" 294", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "10", "atf": "x [x x x i]-ṣa#-ba-at-su₂# [x x]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] will seize him […]"}, {"number": "11", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ... [...] ... [...]\n#note: As noted by @bib{RN2651@12}, these lines appear to parallel OB Ishchali 32′–33′.\n// cf. L I.4 OB \"Ischchali\" 32'\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 304", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "11", "atf": "x [x x x x] ni ip? pu x [x x]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] … […,]"}, {"number": "12", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ... [...] ... | sebet? (|) kiṣrī? | ... [...]\n#note: @bib{RN2651@12} suggests reading @akk{7?# ki?#-iṣ-ri hur!-ša!-ni!}, “seven mountain ranges.”\n// cf. L I.4 OB \"Ischchali\" 33'\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 307", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "12", "atf": "m[a-...] x 7?# ki?#-iṣ-ri ki-x x ba x x x [(x x)]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] @i{seven knots} … […]"}, {"number": "13", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n zizānam | i[nēru | nāʾe]ram | mupparšam | mubatt[iram]\n#note: See @bib{RN117@270}: “The word @i{zi-za-na-am} is curiously written, half on the tablet’s left edge. There are two possible meanings, (a) a kind of grasshopper or locust, well attested, and (b) a half-share or measure known only from the lexical entry @i{MSL} XVI, p. 162, @i{Nabnītu} XVII 238: ½.tar = @i{zi-za-nu}. Which is appropriate here — if either — is uncertain.” The new parallel in SB V 308 suggests the reading adopted [EJ].\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 19\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 308", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "13", "atf": "zi-za-na-am i-[ne₂-ru na-i]-ra-am mu-pa!-ar-ša!-am mu-ba-at#-t[i-ra-am]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: The Cricket they [killed], the Screecher, the Flyer, the Worm,"}, {"number": "14", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ... [...] ...\n#note: See @bib{RN117@270}: “Perhaps @akk{ha-[ar-ha-ra-am ma-ṣa]-ru qi₂-iš-tim}, with OB Ishchali 30', but the rest of the line is obscure.”\n// cf. L I.4 OB \"Ischchali\" 30'", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "14", "atf": "ha-[x x (x)] x-ru x x-tim ba-ṣu x ši im x ab x [x;]-im", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: … […] …"}, {"number": "15", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ... [...] ... | inēr-ma | ... [(...)]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "15", "atf": "i-[x x (x)] x-am x x x-am i-ne₂-er-ma te-ri-ik [(x x)]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: […] … he slew and…,"}, {"number": "16", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n i[nēr] | hamsīšu", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "16", "atf": "i-[ne₂-er?] ha-am-ši-šu-u₂", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: he [@i{smote}] five times."}, {"number": "17a", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ... | irtahiṣ || qištam | ša erēni\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 300", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "17a", "atf": "di#-x# (x#) x# ir#-ta#-hi-iṣ qi₂-iš?-tam <ša> {giš#}EREN?#\n$ line continues", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: …he went trampling through the forest of cedar,"}, {"number": "17b-18", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n mūšab (|) ilī | enunakkī || puzzuram | ipte\n#note: See @bib{RN117@270}: “OB Ishchali is similar (37'–8': @akk{ir-ta-hi-<iṣ>} @i{qištam} / @i{mūšab Enunnakkī puzzuram ipte}), but what precedes and follows is different.”\n// cf. L I.4 OB \"Ischchali\" 38'", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "17b-18", "atf": "mu-ša-bi i-li | e-nu-na-ki pu-zu-ra#-mi ip-te", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: he discovered the secret abode of the Anunnaki gods."}, {"number": "19", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n waldam | ṣērim || mitlukam | ileʾʾi\n// cf. L I.4 OB \"Harmal₂\" 47", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "19", "atf": "wa-al-dam ṣe!-ri#-im# mi-it!-lu-ka-am i-le-ʾi₃", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": true, "translation": "#tr.en: The wild-born was able to give counsel,"}, {"number": "19b", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n issaqar[am] | ana ibrī[šu]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "19b", "atf": "is-sa₃-qa₂-r[a-am] | a-na ib-ri-[šu]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: he said to his friend:"}, {"number": "20", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ina dunnīka-ma | maṣṣaram | tenēram", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "20", "atf": "i-na du-ni-ka-ma ma-ṣa-ra-am te-ne₂-ra-am", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: ‘By your strength alone you slew the guardian,"}, {"number": "21-22a", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n mīnû | ubaššakka || qištam | ša <erēni> | šunēl\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 304", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "21-22a", "atf": "mi-nu-u₂-um u₂-ba-ša-ka qi₂-iš-tam ša {giš}<EREN> | šu-ne₂-el\n$ line continues\n#note: See @bib{RN117@271}: “@akk{GIŠ} is probably defective for @akk{{giš}}@i{erēnim}. More is missing if the line is to make sense as it stands, so I presume that @i{šunēl} belongs at the end and has slipped to l. 22 by mistake.”", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: what can bring you dishonour? The forest of <cedar> wood (22) lay low!"}, {"number": "22b", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n šuwwiam | erēnam | šīham\n#note: See @bib{RN117@271}: “Von Soden (‘die dir nun gehört’) and Hecker (‘deine’) took the second word as the accusative independent possessive pronoun, evidently reading @i{ku-wa-a-am}. However, the expected form in OB is @i{kâm}. Bottéro (‘un Cèdre extraordinairement élevé’) evidently parsed it as the accusative adjective @i{šūpâm} (cf. Tournay and Shaffer: @i{šu-pi-a-am}), but the uncontracted form would be @i{šūpuʾam} not @i{šūpiʾam}. I suppose it to be the verb @i{šeʾûm} in the imperative of the rare II/1 stem, with a glide in place of the glottal stop. This couplet exhibits an emphatic alliteration on /š/ lacking in the later version, which has @i{ibrī nittakis erēna šīha / ša muhhašu šamê nakpu} (SB V 293–4).”\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 314", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "22b", "atf": "šu-wi-a-am {giš}ERIN ši-ha-am\n$ line continues", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: Seek out for me a tall cedar,"}, {"number": "22c", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ša muhhašu | šamāʾī | šannu\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 315", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "22c-23", "atf": "ša mu-ha-šu | ($___$) ša-ma-A.A ša-an-nu", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: whose top vies with the heavens!"}, {"number": "23", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n lūpuš | daltam || ša qanâ | rupussa\n#note: On the specific door described in these lines, and its counterpart in the Standard Babylonian version, see @bib{RN2651@12}.\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 316", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "24", "atf": "lu-pu-uš {giš}IG ša qa₂-na ru-pu-us₂-sa", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: I will make a door whose breadth is a reed-length,"}, {"number": "24", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ay irši | šagammam || sippam | lillik\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 317", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "25", "atf": "a-a ir#-ši?# ša-ga-ma-am si-pa-am li-li-ik?#", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: let it not @i{have} a pivot, let it travel (in) the door jamb."}, {"number": "25", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n amāt (|) lētāša || qanâ | rupussa\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 317", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "26", "atf": "a!(DIŠ)-ma-at le-ta#-ša# qa₂-na ru-pu-us₂-sa", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: Its side will be a cubit, a reed-length its breadth,"}, {"number": "26", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ay iṭhēšim | ahûm || ilum | lirā[mši]", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "27", "atf": "a-a iṭ-he-ši-im a-hu-um i-lu-um li-ra-a[m!-ši]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: may no stranger draw near it, may a god have love for [it!]"}, {"number": "27", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n ana bīti (|) ellil | libil (|) pur[a]ttum\n#note: See @bib{RN117@271}: “As read the genitive construct state @i{bīti} either (a) retains its case-vowel, exhibiting the old-fashioned ending (as in OB II 165), or (b) exhibits crasis, @i{bīt-Illil}. One might instead read @i{qá-ti}, ‘to the hands of Enlil’.”\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 318", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "28", "atf": "a-na bi-ti en-lil₂ li-be₂-el pu-ra-[a]t-tum", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": false, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: To the house of Enlil the Euphrates shall take it,"}, {"number": "28", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n lihdū-ma | ummān | nippuri[m]\n#note: See @bib{RN117@271}: “An alternative but less plausible reading is @akk{li-ih-du u₂-šu-um-gal NIBRU{ki}}, ‘let the dragon of Nippur become glad’.”\n// cf. L I.4 SB \"V\" 319", "manuscripts": [{"manuscriptId": 1, "labels": ["o"], "number": "29", "atf": "li-ih-du-u₂-ma um-ma-an# NIBRU{k[i}]", "omittedWords": []}], "intertext": ""}], "isSecondLineOfParallelism": true, "isBeginningOfSection": false, "translation": "#tr.en: may the folk of Nippur rejoice,"}, {"number": "29", "oldLineNumbers": [], "variants": [{"reconstruction": "%n lirīssim | enli